  #block(breakable: false)[
  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Legal membership, carrying rights and duties. Residence can last a lifetime without citizenship, the vote is one right of many, and tax is a duty rather than the status itself.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Residence alone does not confer citizenship, and the naturalisation route requires fifteen years. Birth, descent and naturalisation are all routes in sections 25 to 27.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Descent. Birth as a route depends on being born in Nigeria to parents or grandparents of an indigenous community.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Registration, under section 26. Naturalisation, under section 27, is the route for a resident of fifteen years who is not married to a citizen.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Fifteen years, together with good character, a language of the community and acceptance by the local community.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Good character, residence, a language of the community and local acceptance are the statutory conditions. Property, party membership and military service are not required.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Dual citizenship is permitted: a Nigerian who acquires another citizenship does not lose the Nigerian one, though a naturalised citizen may be required to renounce a former citizenship.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Paying lawful taxes is a duty. Voting and party membership are rights that a citizen may exercise, and ministerial office is an appointment.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Chapter IV, sections 33 to 46. Chapter II holds the fundamental objectives, which are not enforceable in the courts.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Fair hearing is section 36, in Chapter IV. Employment, education and shelter are Chapter II objectives, and the Constitution says the courts will not enforce them.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 46 gives the High Court jurisdiction to hear such an application. The other bodies neither adjudicate nor remedy a breach.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 33 permits deprivation only in execution of a court sentence in respect of a criminal offence, and in a few other narrow cases such as defence of property.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 39 protects expression, but the law may impose limits for defence, public safety, public order and morality. Incitement is outside the right.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 41 permits restriction by law in the interests of defence, public safety, public order, public morality or public health — the standard limitation clause.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It investigates complaints, visits places of detention and reports. It cannot make binding orders — that is a court's power.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It is Nigeria's ombudsman: it investigates administrative injustice by public bodies and recommends remedies.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Implementation is the core: ministries, departments, agencies and officials carrying policy into effect. Making policy is the politician's function, and adjudication and elections are other institutions'.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Permanence, with anonymity, impartiality and hierarchy. Election belongs to political office, profit to business, and partisanship is precisely what the service must not show.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    They implement the policy of the government of the day, including policies they advised against. They vote like other citizens, can be dismissed for misconduct, and are appointed through the service commissions.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Federal Civil Service Commission, with parallel commissions for the states. The Federal Character Commission polices balance, and the Judicial Service Commission handles judicial officers.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Auditor-General reports to the National Assembly on how money was spent. Legislative committees, the courts, the ombudsman and the Code of Conduct Bureau are the other controls.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Asset declaration, to prevent conflict of interest and unexplained wealth. Party membership, tenure and residence are not its business.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It is created by statute, has its own legal personality and funds, and is run by a board. A ministry department has no separate personality, and a council is a tier of government.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Service where the market will not provide it, natural monopoly, social objectives and strategic control are the reasons. Profit, small government and avoiding accountability are not.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Political interference in management, overstaffing and losses covered by the treasury are the standard problems, and they are the case for privatisation.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 7 guarantees a system of democratically elected local government councils, and the states are to ensure their existence under a law that provides for their powers.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    774. The uniform system dates from the 1976 reform, and the number has grown with state creation since.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Local revenue and local services — markets, roads, sanitation, health posts and primary education support. Defence, currency and federal elections are federal matters.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Statutory allocation, supplemented by a share of state revenue and by internally generated revenue such as rates and tolls.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It created a uniform system of councils across the country — the 301 that have since grown to 774. The FCT was created in the same period but by a separate decision.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Elected, together with the councillors, under section 7's requirement of a democratically elected council. State governors have sometimes appointed caretaker committees, which is the very practice the section is meant to exclude.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Adequate shelter is in Chapter II, section 16. The other three are Chapter IV rights enforceable under section 46.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 42 lists ethnic group, place of origin, sex, religion, political opinion and circumstances of birth. The list is closed, and wealth and age are not on it.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The President may confer citizenship on a person for exceptional service to the nation. It is the rarest route and does not require residence.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Dual citizenship is permitted, so the Nigerian citizenship is retained. A naturalised citizen may be asked to renounce a former citizenship, which is the reverse case.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Continuity is the purpose: a new minister inherits a service that knows the files. Officials do retire, and they are appointed rather than elected.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The minister answers in the House for the ministry's conduct, which is why anonymity for officials and responsibility for ministers go together.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Company income tax is collected by the Federal Inland Revenue Service and paid into the Federation Account; a council receives only its share of the allocation. Tolls, rates and the allocation are its own sources.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Legal personality and managerial flexibility are the merits. It remains accountable through its enabling Act and the ministry, can make losses, and is run by a board rather than directly by the civil service.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Section 6(6)(c) excludes them from direct enforcement. They guide policy, and the courts have sometimes used them as an aid to interpretation, but they are not rights.
  ]

]

